# Dashboard Walkthrough

## Overview

The PM Confirmation Dashboard is designed to provide visibility into project confirmation performance across the organization.

Users can navigate from organization-level KPIs down to individual project details through drill-through interactions.

---

# Navigation Flow

Global Dashboard

↓

Vertical Detail

↓

Project Manager Detail

↓

Project-Level Visibility

---

# Page 1 – Global Dashboard

## Purpose

Provide an executive summary of overall project confirmation performance.

---

## KPI Cards

### Total Projects

Displays the total number of projects currently tracked.

---

### Confirmed Projects

Displays projects with status:

Confirmed

---

### Pending Projects

Displays projects with status:

Yet to be confirmed

---

### Completion Percentage

Displays overall confirmation progress.

---

## Confirmation Status Chart

### Purpose

Displays the distribution between:

* Confirmed Projects
* Pending Projects

### Usage

Quickly identify overall confirmation progress.

---

## Vertical Ranking Visual

### Purpose

Compare performance across business verticals.

### Usage

Identify:

* Top-performing verticals
* Verticals requiring attention

### Interaction

Right-click a vertical and select:

Drill Through → Vertical Detail

---

## Race To 100 Leaderboard

### Purpose

Track Project Manager confirmation performance.

### Usage

Identify:

* Top performers
* Pending confirmations

### Interaction

Right-click a Project Manager and select:

Drill Through → PM Detail

---

# Page 2 – Vertical Detail

## Purpose

Provide detailed performance analysis for a selected vertical.

---

## KPI Cards

Displays:

* Total Projects
* Confirmed Projects
* Pending Projects
* Completion Percentage

for the selected vertical.

---

## PM Performance Table

### Purpose

Compare Project Managers within the selected vertical.

### Columns

* Project Manager
* Total Projects
* Confirmed Projects
* Pending Projects
* Completion Percentage

### Usage

Identify high-performing and low-performing PMs.

---

## Drill-Through

Select a Project Manager and navigate to:

PM Detail

for project-level visibility.

---

# Page 3 – Project Manager Detail

## Purpose

Provide detailed visibility into projects assigned to a selected Project Manager.

---

## KPI Cards

Displays:

* Total Projects
* Confirmed Projects
* Pending Projects
* Completion Percentage

for the selected PM.

---

## Project Detail Table

### Columns

* Project ID
* Project Name
* PM Status

### Usage

Review individual project confirmation status.

